Project Name: GramBazaar – Smart Village Shopping

Act as a senior website developer and UI/UX designer with 15 years of experience in web development, e-commerce, 3D web design, and API integration.

Create a modern, attractive, mobile-responsive, single-page e-commerce website called GramBazaar, designed for Indian village businesses and local customers.

1. Technology

- HTML5
- CSS3
- Vanilla JavaScript
- Three.js for 3D models and animations
- REST API integration using Fetch API
- WhatsApp click-to-chat ordering
- LocalStorage for cart persistence

Deliver a complete, working "index.html" file with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript included.

2. Modern 3D Design

- Create a premium 3D-inspired shopping website.
- Add an interactive 3D rotating shopping box or shopping basket using Three.js.
- Use smooth animations and floating product cards.
- Add attractive hover effects and animated buttons.
- Use a professional green, white, and orange color theme.
- Make the 3D section responsive on mobile devices.
- Display a fallback design if WebGL or Three.js is unavailable.

3. Website Header

Create a responsive navigation bar containing:

- GramBazaar logo
- Home
- All Products
- Categories
- About Us
- Contact Us
- Search bar
- Shopping cart icon with item count
- Mobile hamburger menu

4. Homepage

Create an attractive hero section with:

Headline: "गाँव का बाज़ार, अब आपके मोबाइल पर!"

Subheading: "अपने गाँव और आसपास की दुकानों से पसंदीदा सामान आसानी से ऑर्डर करें।"

Buttons:

- अभी खरीदें
- WhatsApp पर ऑर्डर करें

Include an attractive 3D shopping illustration.

5. Product Categories

Display category cards for:

- किराना सामान
- कपड़े
- फल और सब्जियाँ
- कृषि उत्पाद
- घरेलू सामान
- इलेक्ट्रॉनिक्स

Each category should have an icon, image, and clickable category filter.

6. Product Listing

Display products in a responsive grid.

Each product card must include:

- Product image
- Product name in Hindi
- Price in Indian rupees
- Optional original price and discount
- Quantity selector
- Add to Cart button
- Order on WhatsApp button

Load products dynamically from a JavaScript array or REST API.

Include sample products so the website works immediately without an API.

7. Shopping Cart

Implement a functional shopping cart.

Features:

- Add products to cart
- Increase or decrease quantity
- Remove products
- Calculate subtotal and total
- Display cart item count
- Save cart data in LocalStorage
- Show a checkout form

The checkout form should collect:

- Customer name
- Mobile number
- Delivery address
- Optional village or locality
- Order notes

Validate required fields before submitting the order.

8. WhatsApp Ordering

When the customer clicks Place Order:

1. Validate the checkout form.
2. Collect customer information.
3. Collect all product names, quantities, and prices.
4. Calculate the order total.
5. Generate a formatted Hindi WhatsApp message.
6. Open WhatsApp with the complete order message addressed to the seller.

Example message:

नमस्ते GramBazaar!

मुझे निम्नलिखित सामान ऑर्डर करना है।

ग्राहक का नाम: [Customer Name]
मोबाइल नंबर: [Mobile Number]
पता: [Delivery Address]

ऑर्डर:

1. चावल – 2 किलो – ₹120
2. चीनी – 1 किलो – ₹50

कुल राशि: ₹170

कृपया मेरा ऑर्डर कन्फर्म करें।

Use a configurable seller WhatsApp number in international format without the + sign.

Use the WhatsApp click-to-chat URL with properly encoded message text.

Clearly explain that opening WhatsApp does not automatically send the message; the customer must press Send.

9. API Integration

Create a reusable API integration layer.

Requirements:

- Use JavaScript Fetch API.
- Support GET requests to retrieve products.
- Support POST requests to submit orders to a backend.
- Include loading indicators.
- Handle API errors.
- Show user-friendly Hindi error messages.
- Use sample products if the product API is unavailable.

Create configurable settings:

API_BASE_URL
PRODUCTS_API_ENDPOINT
ORDERS_API_ENDPOINT
SELLER_WHATSAPP_NUMBER

Example endpoints:

GET /api/products
POST /api/orders

Do not invent a working backend. Document the expected API request and response formats.

Keep API configuration separate from UI logic.

Never expose secret API keys in frontend JavaScript. Use a secure backend for private credentials and sensitive operations.

WhatsApp ordering should work independently of the backend API.

